WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.625 --> 00:00:08.542
Two decades of civil war.

00:00:08.709 --> 00:00:12.208
No government.
A haven for international piracy.

00:00:12.375 --> 00:00:14.999
A militant uprising
and a million refugees.

00:00:15.125 --> 00:00:20.375
Somalia has long-been the international
model of a failed state.

00:00:20.542 --> 00:00:22.375
A new president was elected a year ago

00:00:22.542 --> 00:00:25.250
and his government's influence
is starting to take root.

00:00:25.417 --> 00:00:28.625
It's trying to move this impoverished
nation from an emergency

00:00:28.792 --> 00:00:30.542
to a recovery phase.

00:00:30.709 --> 00:00:33.709
But Somalia's challenges,
like its social structure,

00:00:33.875 --> 00:00:35.834
are complex and varied.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:40.291
That's where the EU,
through its comprehensive approach

00:00:40.458 --> 00:00:43.208
to the Horn of Africa,
wants to play a role.

00:00:43.375 --> 00:00:45.583
With three missions, political support

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:47.999
and more than a billion euros
in assistance,

00:00:48.125 --> 00:00:53.083
the EU is trying to help get Somalia
back on the road to recovery.

00:00:53.834 --> 00:00:55.709
Security is the biggest challenge.

00:00:55.875 --> 00:00:58.208
So building up the army
is a high priority.

00:00:58.375 --> 00:01:02.125
It's a big task, that Europe is tackling
through its military training mission,

00:01:02.291 --> 00:01:04.125
EUTM Somalia.

00:01:04.291 --> 00:01:06.583
The presence of EUTM Somalia
in Mogadishu

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:11.709
is most certainly an accelerator as far
as the European Union is concerned,

00:01:11.875 --> 00:01:16.625
establishing
an expanding future foothold

00:01:16.792 --> 00:01:19.208
in Mogadishu
and throughout Somalia.

00:01:19.375 --> 00:01:22.709
It will be able to provide
situational awareness,

00:01:22.875 --> 00:01:26.333
provide logistical support,
force protection support,

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:28.750
to ensure that all of the requirements

00:01:28.917 --> 00:01:33.125
for a secure deployment
of the full spectrum of EU actors,

00:01:33.291 --> 00:01:36.166
both in Mogadishu
and throughout Somalia, is in place.

00:01:37.041 --> 00:01:38.834
To help Somalia defend itself,

00:01:38.999 --> 00:01:42.542
EUTM has moved into the Jazeera camp
in Mogadishu.

00:01:42.709 --> 00:01:44.750
For the last 3 years
the mission has trained

00:01:44.917 --> 00:01:49.875
some 3,000 Somali soldiers and officers
remotely, in Uganda.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:54.917
Trainees will now be lodged here,
in some of the camp's 130 buildings.

00:01:55.959 --> 00:01:59.208
As part of the comprehensive
European approach to state-building,

00:01:59.375 --> 00:02:02.291
EUTM staff also advise
the defence ministry

00:02:02.458 --> 00:02:06.375
and the EU funds
the African peacekeeping force here.

00:02:06.542 --> 00:02:08.125
Work at Jazeera goes on,

00:02:08.291 --> 00:02:12.959
bolstering the camp's perimeter,
with sand bags and watch towers.

00:02:13.083 --> 00:02:16.166
The chief security threat in Somalia
comes from Al-Shebab,

00:02:16.333 --> 00:02:19.250
a hard-line Islamist group
linked to al-Qaeda.

00:02:19.417 --> 00:02:22.041
Fighters routinely launch attacks
in Mogadishu,

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:26.291
to show that they can strike
anywhere, anytime.

00:02:31.250 --> 00:02:35.208
Much of the European Union's political
capital goes into supporting this man,

00:02:35.375 --> 00:02:37.583
President Hassan Sheikh Mohamud.

00:02:39.417 --> 00:02:41.999
This flight offshore
to meet EU commanders

00:02:42.125 --> 00:02:45.834
came the day after
an Al-Shebab attempt on his life.

00:02:46.458 --> 00:02:48.375
The president has been in office a year

00:02:48.542 --> 00:02:51.834
and is working to project his influence
throughout Somalia.

00:02:51.999 --> 00:02:54.583
The New Deal conference
in Brussels in September,

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:57.333
which secured new funds
and international support,

00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:00.667
is set to help his government
restore stability.

00:03:03.417 --> 00:03:06.999
The counter-piracy operation,
EU Naval Force Atalanta,

00:03:07.125 --> 00:03:09.999
is currently run from
the Dutch ship Johan De Witt.

00:03:10.417 --> 00:03:12.125
It's a huge floating dock,

00:03:12.291 --> 00:03:16.792
capable of launching fast boats
to chase down pirate skiffs.

00:03:17.166 --> 00:03:21.125
The Force watches over
one of the world's major shipping areas.

00:03:21.291 --> 00:03:23.041
In fact, we have four tasks.

00:03:23.208 --> 00:03:27.750
First of all, we protect
World Food Programme ships.

00:03:27.917 --> 00:03:30.583
We deter and suppress piracy.

00:03:30.750 --> 00:03:32.792
We protect vulnerable shipping.

00:03:32.959 --> 00:03:36.166
And we contribute to
the monitoring of fishing activities

00:03:36.333 --> 00:03:38.291
off the coast of Somalia.

00:03:38.458 --> 00:03:41.166
The biggest challenge
is the amount of water

00:03:41.333 --> 00:03:47.208
because the size of the area we are
patrolling here is the size of Europe.

00:03:47.959 --> 00:03:53.125
The EU NAVFOR Operation commander has
no doubts about the value of the operation.

00:03:53.291 --> 00:03:57.917
Europe relies on the trade that goes
through the Bab-el-Mandeb straits.

00:03:58.125 --> 00:04:00.709
5,000 ships a month pass through there.

00:04:00.875 --> 00:04:02.667
I should think 80 per cent of that,

00:04:02.834 --> 00:04:05.333
on their way north through there
and up to Suez,

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:08.250
is going to conduct trade with Europe.

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:11.667
If we don't have confidence
in that route

00:04:11.834 --> 00:04:15.125
then, all of a sudden,
one of our key interests is affected.

00:04:17.917 --> 00:04:21.291
International efforts at sea,
the robust patrolling by warships

00:04:21.458 --> 00:04:25.208
combined with the work of private
security firms on cargo vessels,

00:04:25.417 --> 00:04:27.792
have helped to thwart the pirates.

00:04:27.959 --> 00:04:30.583
But much work remains to be done on land

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:35.000
to provide jobless Somalis
with other opportunities.

00:04:36.208 --> 00:04:43.250
What we know is that we have
brought piracy down by 90 per cent.

00:04:43.417 --> 00:04:45.083
That's a great statistic.

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:47.583
But actually
things haven't changed ashore.

00:04:47.959 --> 00:04:51.625
The networks are still in place
and if we take the pressure off

00:04:51.792 --> 00:04:56.917
there's no reason why piracy won't
re-emerge as a difficult issue for us.

00:04:57.083 --> 00:05:00.250
So we've got to stay here
until the seas are controlled.

00:05:02.999 --> 00:05:05.000
Given Somalia's security challenges,

00:05:05.166 --> 00:05:09.250
ships like the Johan De Witt are also
being used as floating classrooms,

00:05:09.417 --> 00:05:13.667
to help tackle the problems of piracy
closer to the shore.

00:05:13.834 --> 00:05:15.291
In the safety of these vessels,

00:05:15.458 --> 00:05:19.125
the EUCAP Nestor mission
is helping to build up the coastguard.

00:05:19.291 --> 00:05:23.667
Staff train police and customs officers,
in an effort to contain the problem

00:05:23.834 --> 00:05:28.750
before any would-be pirates
make it out to international waters.

00:05:31.667 --> 00:05:34.999
In the Somali basin
EU Naval Force personnel head out

00:05:35.125 --> 00:05:38.583
to round up suspects
and question boat owners.

00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:42.999
They build up a database of information
that will help identify repeat offenders

00:05:43.125 --> 00:05:47.000
and pinpoint the source of
the piracy problem.

00:05:48.792 --> 00:05:52.166
In an exercise on deck,
Somalia's top justice officials

00:05:52.333 --> 00:05:55.625
are taught about European
evidence gathering techniques.

00:05:55.792 --> 00:05:58.959
This is knowledge they can use
to collect, handle and process

00:05:59.083 --> 00:06:01.667
materials found at
a potential crime scene.

00:06:02.583 --> 00:06:07.291
It's expertise they can use
when pirates face them in court.

00:06:07.583 --> 00:06:10.667
Our job is to gather evidence

00:06:10.834 --> 00:06:13.792
and to deliver it to a court
and they will decide.

00:06:14.000 --> 00:06:16.709
It's just one part of
EUCAP Nestor's work,

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:21.875
but it's all part of shifting the focus
from piracy at sea back to the land,

00:06:22.625 --> 00:06:25.166
where extremes of poverty,
climate and ideology

00:06:25.333 --> 00:06:27.583
created the problem in the first place.

00:06:27.750 --> 00:06:31.709
Our success with piracy,
and the changes in Somalia

00:06:31.875 --> 00:06:33.792
with the federal Somali government,

00:06:33.959 --> 00:06:37.875
mean that there's space and time now
to look at this problem ashore.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:42.166
The roots of the piracy problem
lie ashore, the symptoms lie at sea.

00:06:42.333 --> 00:06:44.917
So we need to really get to
the heart of this disease.

00:06:45.959 --> 00:06:49.875
And at the heart of this disease
lie problems of unemployment,

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:51.875
particularly among young men.

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:54.208
Many jobs were lost in
the fishing sector,

00:06:54.375 --> 00:06:57.709
due to piracy and
illegal fishing by foreigners.

00:06:57.875 --> 00:07:01.834
One of the issues is
how do we deal with these boys.

00:07:01.999 --> 00:07:04.875
Can we provide
an alternative way of life

00:07:05.000 --> 00:07:10.250
so that they will not attempt
to venture out onto the sea again?

00:07:10.542 --> 00:07:13.333
The European Union
has invested

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:19.875
a lot of money in that area
and that issue is now being dealt with.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:23.208
And the EU funds, the EU expertise,

00:07:23.375 --> 00:07:28.458
will all be facilitating
the pushing of Somalia towards that.

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:32.750
Through its civilian
and military operations,

00:07:32.917 --> 00:07:35.166
development assistance
and political support,

00:07:35.333 --> 00:07:38.750
the European Union is trying
to help get Somalis back to work

00:07:39.041 --> 00:07:41.959
by providing security and investment.

00:07:42.083 --> 00:07:46.333
It's the hope of a better life that
might starve Al-Shebab of recruits

00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:50.750
and keep young men off the high seas.

